			<outline text="worknotes.md">
				<outline text="#### 11/28/26; 10:07:31 AM by DW -- v0.6.58">
					<outline text="&lt;i&gt;Open local file&lt;/i&gt; command in File menu. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Workaround a GitHub historic feature. When we ask for a Markdown file it sends back an HTML file. We are probably the only app that wants the Markdown version. We watch for this specific situation and correct the mistake. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="A bon:// address typed into the address bar now works. ">
						<outline text="* Try: `bon://scripting.com/code/mymarkdown/index.md`">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="Right-click in address bar shows a menu with Cut, Copy, Paste and go, Select All.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 11/22/26; 10:46:55 AM by DW">
					<outline text="Lots of small changes [outlined here](https://github.com/scripting/bonBon/issues/16). ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 11/21/26; 10:25:43 AM by DW">
					<outline text="Uploaded a downloadable [snapshot](https://github.com/scripting/bonBon/blob/main/demos/brentbloginmarkdown/readme.md) of the inessential.com blog by Brent Simmons. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="How to link to sites for now: First point to the Markdown source, for people who aren't reading from the BonBon browser, they will see the Markdown source which is exactly what you'd expect for a historic browser like Safari. Nod your head and move on. But if you're reading it in BonBon, you see a nicely rendered Markdown page. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Demo:">
						<outline text="*  Introducing &lt;a href=&quot;https://brent.writersweb.org/&quot;&gt;brent.writersweb.org&lt;/a&gt;, as &lt;a href=&quot;https://demo.bonbonweb.org/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbrent.writersweb.org%2F&quot;&gt;viewed&lt;/a&gt; in BonBon. ">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="It took a while to figure this out, and it's hard to anticipate something like this before shipping. In general we want people to get both the Markdown pointer, and a pointer linked into demo.bonbonweb.org. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 11/20/26; 8:32:16 AM by DW">
					<outline text="We should have an RSS 2.0 feed for updates, but for now this worknotes.md file will have to do. I will try to keep it current. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Version 0.6.55 is released. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Files ending with .js or .json are rendered as listings. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="New [demo](https://github.com/scripting/bonBon/blob/main/demos/bloginmarkdown/readme.md) with the Markdown source for the Scripting News in Markdown website, a snapshot from yesterday. Should provide a decent example for developers trying to convert the output of a CMS from HTML to Markdown.  ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Main feature -- this is the first release where we have released the JavaScript code for the Electron app.  ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="We're using the MIT License. I want there to be quick growth in the Markdown web, and this is a way to drive it. We will keep moving the app forward, lots of plans for things to do here, and at least one of them will come out in the next few days. I am serious about doing for text what we did for talk radio with podcasting. And we're looking for people to fill in the blank areas, we could use some serious Markdown editors with storage, designed for publishing apps. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 11/19/26; 6:57:03 PM by DW">
					<outline text="As part of getting BonBon ready for the world, we converted a few websites from HTML to Markdown. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Not just the files, but the structures -- the home page, the monthly archive, daily pages, and story pages and more. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="I'm seeing people start to experiment with making their own sites. I want to show them how we did it with Scripting News.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="#### This is [where you go](https://github.com/scripting/bonBon/blob/main/demos/bloginmarkdown/readme.md). ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 11/19/26; 2:48:53 PM by DW">
					<outline text="The Mac app has its icon back, the Black Lab, which 0.6.52 and 0.6.53 shipped without. It's back in 0.6.54. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="A bon:// link is a link that opens in BonBon. Click one in Chrome, in email, anywhere on the Mac, and BonBon comes to the front showing that page. Example below. ">
						<outline text="* bon://dave.writersweb.org/worknotes.md">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="The startup script calls hitCounter function. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 11/18/26; 5:16:23 PM by DW -- v0.6.53">
					<outline text="A page that a server sends zipped now shows as a normal page.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="On reload the text stays in place, it no longer jumps to the left edge and back.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="The brief clear between pages is gone, the old page stays until the new one replaces it.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="The Markdown copy of Scripting News now takes its posts from the feed, and hears about a new one from FeedLand’s socket.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="The Mac app is now signed with a Developer ID and checked by Apple, so macOS opens it without saying it’s damaged.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 11/18/26; 10:41:19 AM by DW">
